{#
  NetworkPolicy for an *arr slice-2 ingress rule — sonarr and radarr's networkpolicy.yaml.j2
  share this exact structure (podSelector on `app: <name>`, traefik admitted unconditionally,
  a caller matchExpressions list, one TCP port) and differ only in the caller list and its
  per-item comments. Those stay at the call site via `{% call %}` rather than being swallowed
  here — the whole point of the comments is that they differ role to role: sonarr annotates
  every caller, radarr only prowlarr and homepage. Do not harmonize the two call sites to make
  them look more alike; the macro exists to hold the structure both already share, not to grow
  the shared surface.

  prowlarr's own networkpolicy.yaml.j2 is NOT this shape and is NOT converted: it's
  flaresolverr's policy (podSelector `app: flaresolverr`, one caller `app: prowlarr`, no
  traefik entry, no matchExpressions list, port from `prowlarr_k8s_flaresolverr_port`) — a
  different subject with a different shape, not this policy under a different name.

  Arguments:
    name  Service/pod `app` label this policy selects, and the NetworkPolicy's own name.
    port  TCP port the caller list is scoped to (`container_item.port` at both call sites).

  Call with a body holding the `values:` list — one `- <caller>` line per entry, indented to
  column 18 (the list's own column) with an optional trailing `# comment`, exactly as it reads
  today in sonarr/radarr's own files. Call plain (no `{% call %}`) only if a future third site
  has no callers to list, which neither current site does.
#}
{% macro arr_networkpolicy(name, port) -%}
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: {{ name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: {{ name }}
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
  ingress:
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app: traefik
        - podSelector:
            matchExpressions:
              - key: app
                operator: In
                values:
{% if caller is defined %}{{ caller() }}{% endif %}
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: {{ port }}
{% endmacro %}
